  "notes": [
    "Haarlemmerweg 91 (pand 0363100012091729, built 1992): the corner block of the four identical 1992 blocks at Haarlemmerweg 91-109, on the corner of the Van Limburg Stirumstraat, five storeys, 14.9 m.",
    "walls[0] the Haarlemmerweg front (panel 0, crops w02-359L 2021-03-22 and w02-359 2025-06-18, square on): buff brick storeys 1-3 between a red-brown ground and top storey, one white bay-window stack at the east end, a wide window at the west end, the stair slot in the middle bay, shop windows and the glazed entrance on the ground.",
    "walls[1] the Van Limburg Stirumstraat side (panel 8, crops w01-89L 2019-01-07 and w01-89 2025-06-18): six bays, two recessed loggias with rounded white balconies (bays 0 and 3), a row of glazed shopfronts under a pale fascia on the ground (plinth).",
    "NOT DRAWN (kit cannot say): the loggias' rounded balcony fronts (drawn straight); the open roof-terrace frames over the loggias in the top storey; the pale fascia band over the shopfronts; the stair slot as one tall light.",
    "Measured 2026-10-25 (measure.ts, evidence in measured.json): groups 0 take the photo's wall and glass colour, window shape, bay count and front class.",
    "Lit colour (2026-10-25 integrator review): the fronts face north and no usable sunlit crop exists (the sunlit 2025 east crop of 91 is 71 pct washed out), so the brightest north reading (99-103, 2020-02-07: buff #8b775e, red-brown #75564c) is used for all four identical blocks and left unmeasured, so the export brightens it like any shaded wall."
